<div class="content">

  <p>HTTP Custom VPN is one of the most powerful apps for tunneling internet using custom payloads and configs. With it, you can access free internet on networks, bypass restrictions, or connect securely. In this complete tutorial, I will guide you through <strong>everything you need to know about HTTP Custom VPN</strong> — from downloading the app, creating payloads, importing configs, and safe usage tips.</p>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>📌 What is HTTP Custom VPN?</h2>

    <p>HTTP Custom is a free VPN app for Android that allows users to use <strong>SSH, SSL, and custom payload tunneling</strong>. It works by using specially crafted payloads that trick your ISP into giving you internet access even without an active data bundle. Apart from bypass tricks, it is also used for:</p>

    <ul>

      <li>Encrypting internet traffic for privacy</li>

      <li>Using SSH and SSL tunneling for secure browsing</li>

      <li>Free internet tricks with payload and host injection</li>

      <li>Importing VPN config files made by experts</li>

      <li>Bypassing app or site restrictions</li>

    </ul>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>📥 Step 1: Download and Install HTTP Custom VPN</h2>

    <p>Download the latest version of HTTP Custom VPN from a trusted source:</p>

    <p><a href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=xyz.easypro.httpcustom" target="_blank">Download HTTP Custom VPN (Google Play)</a></p>

    <p>After downloading, install and open the app. Make sure to allow permissions for internet access and storage (for importing configs).</p>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>⚙️ Step 2: Understanding the Interface</h2>

    <p>When you open HTTP Custom, you will see several options:</p>

    <ul>

      <li><strong>Payload Generator</strong> – to create custom payloads with headers and hosts.</li>

      <li><strong>SSH Settings</strong> – for entering SSH account details.</li>

      <li><strong>Config Import</strong> – for importing ready-made config files.</li>

      <li><strong>Start Button</strong> – to connect to VPN.</li>

    </ul>

    <p>Don’t worry if it looks complicated. I’ll explain each part step by step.</p>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>📡 Step 3: Creating a Custom Payload</h2>

    <p>Payloads are the backbone of HTTP Custom VPN. They act as “commands” that connect your device to hidden gateways for free internet. Here’s how to make one:</p>

    <ul>

      <li>Open <strong>Payload Generator</strong>.</li>

      <li>Enter <strong>URL/Host</strong> (e.g., <code>m.youtube.com</code> or <code>free.facebook.com</code>).</li>

      <li>Select <strong>Request Method</strong> → <code>CONNECT</code> or <code>GET</code>.</li>

      <li>Enable <strong>Keep Alive</strong> and <strong>Online Host</strong>.</li>

      <li>Click <strong>Generate</strong>.</li>

    </ul>

    <p>Example payload:</p>

    <pre>

CONNECT [host_port] HTTP/1.1

Host: m.youtube.com

Connection: Keep-Alive

    </pre>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>🔑 Step 4: SSH Account Setup</h2>

    <p>To use tunneling, you’ll need a free SSH account. Here’s how:</p>

    <ul>

      <li>Visit <a href="https://fastssh.com" target="_blank">FastSSH</a> or <a href="https://sshkit.com" target="_blank">SSHKit</a>.</li>

      <li>Create a free account by selecting your server (choose nearest to your country).</li>

      <li>Copy the details: <strong>Host, Username, Password, Port</strong>.</li>

      <li>Go back to HTTP Custom → <strong>SSH Settings</strong> → Enter details.</li>

    </ul>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>📂 Step 5: Importing Config Files</h2>

    <p>If you don’t want to create payloads manually, you can import configs:</p>

    <ul>

      <li>Download ready-made <code>.hc</code> files from trusted sources (Telegram groups, tech blogs).</li>

      <li>Open HTTP Custom → Tap <strong>Config</strong> → Import.</li>

      <li>Select the downloaded file.</li>

    </ul>

    <p>Once imported, click <strong>Start</strong> and you’re connected!</p>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>🔒 Step 6: Safe Usage Tips</h2>

    <ul>

      <li>Never use public configs from unknown sources (may contain trackers).</li>

      <li>Use SSH accounts with a validity of 3–7 days for stability.</li>

      <li>Always clear cache if the app crashes.</li>

      <li>Don’t use free internet tricks for illegal activities.</li>

    </ul>

  </div>

  <div class="section">

    <h2>📝 Final Thoughts</h2>

    <p>HTTP Custom VPN is one of the best tools for tunneling internet and discovering free browsing tricks. By following this tutorial, you can set up your own payloads, use SSH accounts, and import configs easily. Bookmark this page because I will keep updating new payloads and working configs.</p>

    <p>Next time, I’ll share <strong>exclusive ready-made HTTP Custom configs for different networks</strong> so you don’t need to create them from scratch.</p>

